core/libexpr - C port of trivnote-libexpr

Reads (and, eventually, writes) the same R7RS-ish S-expressions as
the Java library, so that iOS and Qt/X11 frontends can share the
data format.  This was my bad idea; don't blame Claude for this...

Here is a cool idea called "out-of-tree" builds.  Basically you
can keep the source tree clean on a system without the luxury of
running Git.  The idea is as follows:

    ./bootstrap                 # generate ./configure; Git only!
    mkdir /tmp/b && cd /tmp/b   # out-of-tree builds are encouraged
    ${OLDPWD}/configure [CFLAGS=...] [--prefix=...]
    make && make install

LGPL version 3 or later for this guy too.
